@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: Homepage Permissioning
	Frontend testing for viewing the Zendesk Homepage as various users

Teardown:
	* I teardown users with the following userExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| User1 |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Organization1 |

Scenario: View Homepage as Customer
	Customers should be able to view all options available to customer users.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved                   |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1        |
	| Tags             | liferay_dxp,liferay_portal |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                       |
	| Shared Comments  | true                       |
	| SLA              | Gold                       |
	| Tier             | Regular                    |
	| Support Region   | US                         |
	| Support Language | English                    | 
	| External ID      | Organization1              |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer                     |
	| Password         | zendeskqauser                    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | 555-555-5555                     |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       | 
	| External ID      | User1                            | 
	When I log into zendesk as "zendesk.user1@liferay.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	Then I should see the homepage as a customer
	And the current language should be listed as "ENGLISH (US)"

